{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1487995-ignorance-was-bliss-knowing-unveiling-spells-in-everyday-life","id":1487995,"title":"Ignorance WAS Bliss - Knowing/Unveiling Spells In Everyday Life","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-26T03:06:34-07:00","id":1487995,"title":"Ignorance WAS Bliss - Knowing/Unveiling Spells In Everyday Life","content":"Knowing and Unveiling spells are the humble workhorses of the Arcana; you always want the most information possible for the best results. However, knowledge doesn't always bring joy. What Knowing or Unveiling spells do you personally consider to have the highest potential for mundane nightmare fuel?<br /> <br /> Personally, I would be most scarred by Web of Life. I have NO desire to know how many roaches are nearby at a given time. Max-strength Repel would be active at all times.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Mind spells? I'm already insecure, not much would change. <br /> Prime &quot;Truth&quot; spells? Might actually help with that insecurity. <br /> Death? Better to know than live in fear. <br /> Fate? Every Destiny has a bane. <br /> Forces? Seems like it would be trippy and kinda fun. <br /> Matter? Mostly practical, nothing hugely scarring beyond how much fecal matter is in a given item of food<br /> Space? Seems pretty useful, all things considered.<br /> Spirit? Esoteric enough to not fill me with mundane terror. Rot/decay spirits or insect spirits might make it a close second though.<br /> Time? Really bloody useful.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T05:52:34-07:00","id":1488008,"title":"","content":"Fate could potentially cause some with <i>Serendipity</i>. You become able to give good advice, really good advice, even over the phone. You always know a random activity that helps people get out of a rut, and you give weird hints that turn out to make things easier using skills the person is passionate about.<br /> <br /> Problem is that they are not guaranteed to be the easiest or safest ideas, eventually someone could suffer trauma due to it or worse, because they didn't have the common sense to deal with certain twists that could occur.<br /> <br /> Maybe you end up creating a Sin Eater because of it. Best case scenario, the guilt will haunt you. Worst case scenario, they have a vendetta and all the blood spilled is on your hands, and you may be on their list too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-26-2022, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T01:04:19-07:00","id":1488140,"title":"","content":"You know, if you gain Initiation in each of the Arcana and find a supernatural community to sell your services cheaply to then you might become a little famous for being nearly omniscient. Maybe use a Time spell to do the work more quickly or use Space to grant your senses over the phone. <br /> <br /> If we are talking about vampires then that means outclassing an entire Clan. I doubt even the Elders will have enough Devotions to match, and vampires have little guidance into other realms anyway.<br /> <br /> If we are talking about werewolves then the pack that has you will probably never know surprise within their territory. I would develop something to track the corruption of Wounds and cast it on everyone. Obviously, care would need to be to not get scape-goated by Bale Hounds. <br /> <br /> Prometheans don't really have a community exactly. <br /> <br /> If we are talking about changelings then the local goblin market will need to be learn integrity in deals or get rid of you. The question remains if you can easily track the hearts of Huntsmen, or the secrets of Gentry Titles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T01:55:41-07:00","id":1488145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1487995-ignorance-was-bliss-knowing-unveiling-spells-in-everyday-life?p=1488008#post1488008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate could potentially cause some with <i>Serendipity</i>. You become able to give good advice, really good advice, even over the phone. You always know a random activity that helps people get out of a rut, and you give weird hints that turn out to make things easier using skills the person is passionate about.<br /> <br /> Problem is that they are not guaranteed to be the easiest or safest ideas, eventually someone could suffer trauma due to it or worse, because they didn't have the common sense to deal with certain twists that could occur.<br /> <br /> Maybe you end up creating a Sin Eater because of it. Best case scenario, the guilt will haunt you. Worst case scenario, they have a vendetta and all the blood spilled is on your hands, and you may be on their list too.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, guilt could hang heavy depending on how you use it. Fate seems like the Arcana that's really easy to power trip on, with pretty serious consequences when you misjudge something. Even the lowest level of Fate spells are pretty abusable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1487995-ignorance-was-bliss-knowing-unveiling-spells-in-everyday-life?p=1488140#post1488140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>What... did any of that have to do with the question?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T02:12:22-07:00","id":1488148,"title":"","content":"Probably a good idea to not give into the temptation to Divine how people close to you are going to die.<br /> <br /> With Mind, my perspective goes to how there are a lot more people who are privately terrible than one might assume. You look into statistics of how various sorts of abuse happen, and it makes me think that going around casually casting Mental Scan on people with queries concerning their mood, motives, or similar elements has better odds than you might want of being given a flash of something horrifying going on behind closed doors. Even apart from potentially being haunted by the question of &quot;should I do anything about this, and if so what&quot;, the description of how the information is conveyed seems as though it would be highly unpleasant in its own right, and I think it can be existentially fraught to use such magic to realise how many people like that are around you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T02:21:50-07:00","id":1488149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1487995-ignorance-was-bliss-knowing-unveiling-spells-in-everyday-life?p=1488148#post1488148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably a good idea to not give into the temptation to Divine how people close to you are going to die.<br /> <br /> With Mind, my perspective goes to how there are a lot more people who are privately terrible than one might assume. You look into statistics of how various sorts of abuse happen, and it makes me think that going around casually casting Mental Scan on people with queries concerning their mood, motives, or similar elements has better odds than you might want of being given a flash of something horrifying going on behind closed doors. Even apart from potentially being haunted by the question of &amp;quot;should I do anything about this, and if so what&amp;quot;, the description of how the information is conveyed seems as though it would be highly unpleasant in its own right, and I think it can be existentially fraught to use such magic to realise how many people like that are around you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair assessment. The Core book does make a deliberate point that Mastigoi tend to become very disillusioned with humanity as a whole, which tracks with the easy use of Mind magic. <br /> <br /> It <i>is</i> important to note that amoral thoughts don't necessarily translate into amoral actions or abuse - Pink Elephant thoughts are annoyingly memetic by nature. Although that's in the real world, so in-game it would likely skew in the opposite direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T05:42:27-07:00","id":1488158,"title":"","content":"Forces could be used to gain a tremorsense comparable to Toph's from Avatar. This would let you detect what is going on around you in much greater detail, which includes violence, any kidnap victims, people being followed or watched, and many more things hidden behind the scenes. <br /> <br /> With <i>Receiver</i>, they can hear everything going around them. Every rumor and whisper behind their back, the robbers planning a heist in the basement of the room across the street, the mafiosos planning to shoot someone and the corrupt cop taking a bribe.<br /> <br /> Then they start using <i>Tune In</i> to parse through data transmissions, discovering backroom deals, emails from unknown higher ups going to people like janitors or cashiers, hints of something being setup for the dark web, messages you are sure hide terrible things under code words and all the things everyone around you is searching and talking about.<br /> <br /> Forces can give a lot of information, almost too much, maybe enough that you would need to multitask with Mind to parse through it all. All of that requiring no mics, listening devices or traceable software (maybe that is how Guardian spooks learn so much about Sanctums without touching anything). <br /> <br /> But it also shows you how fragile your mundane life is, how so many layers of danger and corruption are much closer to home than expected.<br /> <br /> Now you know, now you can be prepared. But the people around you don't. Can you even afford to drop those spells, for their sake and yours ? What is your responsibility for having this knowledge? You can't hint how you got it, you were warned about mixing your Shadow and mundane persona, but how can you help without exposing how you got such a detailed amount of data, and will that paint a target on you ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-27-2022, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T05:50:57-07:00","id":1488160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1487995-ignorance-was-bliss-knowing-unveiling-spells-in-everyday-life?p=1488158#post1488158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces could be used to gain a tremorsense comparable to Toph's from avatar. This would let you detect what is going on around you in much greater detail, which includes violence, any kidnap victims, people being followed or watched, and many more things hidden behind the scenes. <br /> <br /> With <i>Receiver</i>, they can hear everything going around them. Every rumor and whisper behind their back, the robbers planning a heist in the basement of the room across the street, the mafiosos planning to shoot someone and the corrupt cop taking a bribe.<br /> <br /> Then they start using <i>Tune In</i> to parse through data transmissions, discovering backroom deals, emails from unknown higher ups going to people like janitors or cashiers, hints of something being setup for the dark web, messages you are sure hide terrible things under code words and all the things everyone around you is searching and talking about.<br /> <br /> Forces can give a lot of information, almost too much, maybe enough that you would need to multitask with Mind to parse through it all. All of that requiring no mics, listening devices or traceable software (maybe that is how Guardian spooks learn so much about Sanctums without touching anything). <br /> <br /> But it also shows you how fragile your mundane life, how so many layers of danger and corruption are much closer to home than expected.<br /> <br /> Now you know, now you can be prepared. But the people around you don't. Can you even afford to drop those spells, for their sake and yours ? What is your responsibility for having this knowledge? You can't hint how you got it, you were warned about mixing your Shadow and mundane persona, but how can you help without exposing how you got such a detailed amount of data, and will that paint a target on you ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Mutable Mask, Shadow Name, Occultation, and Incognito Presence are for! What's the point of having magic if you can't act like a superhero now and then?<br /> <br /> (I jest, but I guarantee at least one Arrow or Free Councilor has done the masked vigilante thing. Maybe not the Superman thing, but definately the Batman or Sandman thing.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T06:53:19-07:00","id":1488165,"title":"","content":"In the Guardians book, there is someone who tried. He used a leather coat, an oni mask, a curved sword (the handle looked like that of a tulwar), hyper speed and blue flames. <br /> <br /> He rushed in to save a woman who was being attacked by a vampire. Then he saw it dissolve, the illusion ended, and the woman started greeting him. His senses began to fade as he heard that, once he woke up, they were going to have a chat about using all that flashy magic. <br /> <br /> So if a mage is going to be a vigilante, they better be aware that the Guardian are still watching for breaches of the Veil. Plus they need to be cautious, naivete will get them killed, eventually someone will setup a trap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T12:37:41-07:00","id":1488194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1487995-ignorance-was-bliss-knowing-unveiling-spells-in-everyday-life?p=1488165#post1488165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Guardians book, there is someone who tried. He used a leather coat, an oni mask, a curved sword (the handle looked like that of a tulwar), hyper speed and blue flames. <br /> <br /> He rushed in to save a woman who was being attacked by a vampire. Then he saw it dissolve, the illusion ended, and the woman started greeting him. His senses began to fade as he heard that, once he woke up, they were going to have a chat about using all that flashy magic. <br /> <br /> So if a mage is going to be a vigilante, they better be aware that the Guardian are still watching for breaches of the Veil. Plus they need to be cautious, naivete will get them killed, eventually someone will setup a trap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, thats why you emulate Batman or Sandman - either take things down from a distance, or wade in with subtle and explainable magic. Honing The Form and Enhance Skill for hand-to-hand capabilitirs,, and Sleep of the Just administered via Sleeper hold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-27-2022, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T13:28:35-07:00","id":1488203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1487995-ignorance-was-bliss-knowing-unveiling-spells-in-everyday-life#post1487995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I would be most scarred by Web of Life. I have NO desire to know how many roaches are nearby at a given time. Max-strength Repel would be active at all times.</div> </div> </div> </div>A slight digression, but an interesting corollary to your idea is that the Paths probably make up for a lot of the issues raised by their Arcana.<br /> <br /> Like, the perspective that the Thyrsus path forces/brings out of you, means you probably no longer care much about roaches. Just another of facet of Life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T13:44:14-07:00","id":1488204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1487995-ignorance-was-bliss-knowing-unveiling-spells-in-everyday-life?p=1488203#post1488203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A slight digression, but an interesting corollary to your idea is that the Paths probably make up for a lot of the issues raised by their Arcana.<br /> <br /> Like, the perspective that the Thyrsus path forces/brings out of you, means you probably no longer care much about roaches. Just another of facet of Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. I'd see it more as &quot;I rule Beasts, I shall not fear what I can drive away at a whim&quot;. Which opens all kinds of possibilities for a foe using animal minions to spy on you.<br /> <br /> Of course, every Mage likely has a different take on their Path","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T14:38:24-07:00","id":1488213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1487995-ignorance-was-bliss-knowing-unveiling-spells-in-everyday-life?p=1488204#post1488204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly. I'd see it more as &quot;I rule Beasts, I shall not fear what I can drive away at a whim&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Signs of Sorcery</i> seems pretty explicit about the way that the Thyrsus Path shapes your viewpoint. You don't rule beasts; that implies beasts are an external phenomena, rather than simply small elements of a grander entity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T14:45:40-07:00","id":1488214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1487995-ignorance-was-bliss-knowing-unveiling-spells-in-everyday-life?p=1488213#post1488213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> seems pretty explicit about the way that the Thyrsus Path shapes your viewpoint. You don't rule beasts; that implies beasts are an external phenomena, rather than simply small elements of a grander entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, fair. I'll admit, Thrysus and Moros are the Paths I pay the least attention to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T00:25:57-07:00","id":1488246,"title":"","content":"Still, in interests of character diversity, I could see a Thyrsus within whom there's a conflict between a newfound appreciation for the life that certain creatures possess and their place within a greater ecology, and their personal enduring sense of discomfort.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining an Obrimos who started off being too into looking at just how much energy is constantly going around because of how stimulating it was, but soon found a sense of anxiety to perceive in such detail how much strength is resting just short of colliding with people's fragile bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 07-28-2022, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}